{{ steps (printf "Order #%d" .ID.Num) "pay" }}

{{- /*
The pay area, and no box around it for an on-chain order.

The two halves below are panels in their own right. Wrapped in a third they
were a border inside a border inside a border, which is what a page looks
like when every part of it was written separately.
*/ -}}
{{if and .PayURI .OnChain -}}
## Pay {{ money .Total }} — {{.TotalDCR}}

{{template "paypanel.tmpl" .}}

{{- /*
How long the amount is good for, in a box of its own.

It was a sentence at the end of a paragraph, which is where a reader looking
at a square to scan is not. A line in the theme's own warning colour is read
before anything is decided -- and this is the one thing on the page that runs
out.
*/}}
{{- /*
The clock, counted where there is one.

The page said "another 21 minutes" and went on saying it: a page is fetched
once and nothing tells it the time. At nought it stops being a warning and
becomes what happened, with one press to start again at today's rate. See
markdown_countdown.dart.
*/}}
{{ with .ExpiresInSeconds }}
--countdown[seconds={{.}}, link=/reorder/{{ $.ID }}, label=Order it again]--
{{ end }}
{{- else -}}
{{if .PayURI -}}
## Pay {{ money .Total }} — {{.TotalDCR}}

{{- /*
The one press, in a card of its own.

It was a bare invoice line inside the heading's panel with a sentence under
it saying that pressing it paid. A press that spends money should not need
explaining, and the reassurance about what Lightning is belongs where the
rest of this page keeps its reassurance: behind the question mark.
*/}}
--panel[full=on, padding=16, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=accent, radius=8, text=center, help=Paid from the Bison Relay wallet in this app. Lightning settles the moment it goes through, so the seller sees it immediately and there is nothing to wait for.]--
**Pay with your Bison Relay wallet**

{{ .PayURI }}
--/panel--

{{- /*
The clock, counted where there is one.

The page said "another 21 minutes" and went on saying it: a page is fetched
once and nothing tells it the time. At nought it stops being a warning and
becomes what happened, with one press to start again at today's rate. See
markdown_countdown.dart.
*/}}
{{ with .ExpiresInSeconds }}
--countdown[seconds={{.}}, link=/reorder/{{ $.ID }}, label=Order it again]--
{{ end }}
{{- else -}}
--panel[full=on, padding=16, margin=0 0 16 0, border=1, color=accent, radius=8]--
## Order placed

The seller will be in touch with how to pay.
--/panel--
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

--panel[padding=16, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
{{range .Cart.Items}}
--listing--
title: {{ .Product.Title }}
summary: {{ .Quantity }} × {{ money .Product.Price }}
meta: {{ money .Total }}
{{ with productImage .Product.Image }}image: {{.}}
{{ end -}}
--/listing--
{{end}}
{{ if gt .ShipCharge 0.0 }}Items: {{ money .Cart.Total }} · Shipping: {{ money .ShipCharge }}
{{ end }}### Total: {{ money .Total }} — {{.TotalDCR}}

At {{ printf "%.2f" .ExchangeRate }} USD/DCR
--/panel--
